  ],
  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The area, <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, of a rectangle is given by the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> represents the length of the rectangle and <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> represents its width. It&rsquo;s given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> inches and a width of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> inches. Substituting <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> in the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"upper A equals left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 6 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"upper A equals 42\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>42</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Thus, the area, in square inches, of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum, not the product, of the length and width of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is twice the area, in square inches, of the rectangle.</p>",
